    "stage": "return",
    "payload": {
     "text": "Sunlight looks white, but it is a mix of every color. When it passes through the air, tiny gas molecules scatter short blue wavelengths much more than long red ones. That scattered blue light reaches your eyes from every direction, so the whole sky looks blue. At sunset, light crosses much more air, so most of the blue is scattered away and reds remain.",
